// design system's Icon set (20px grid, 1.5 stroke, round caps and joins) --
// edit the generator, not this file.
//
// Slint's `Path` takes SVG path data, so `<circle>` / `<rect>` are rewritten as
// path commands. A DS element filled with `stroke="none"` is inset by half the
// stroke and drawn stroked *and* filled, so its edge lands where the DS draws
// it; that keeps every glyph's stroke string non-empty and unique, which is
// what `AppIcon`'s lookups key on.
//
// Suffixes: `-solid` is the glyph's filled layer, `-a` / `-b` the part that
// moves on hover (the DS's `lb-i-a` / `lb-i-b`), `-a-solid` that part's fill.
// `AppIcon` finds all of them from `commands` alone, so a consumer only ever
// passes `Icons.<name>`.
//
// Every `Path` here narrows its viewbox by the stroke (t260928-d906): slint's
// default `fit: contain` fits the viewbox into the box *minus* the stroke width
// and shifts it by half of it (`i-slint-core` `items/path.rs`), which drew the
// 20px set at 92.5 % and the 16px one at 90.6 %. A viewbox of
// `grid - weight / unit`, starting at `weight / unit / 2`, cancels that, so a
// grid unit is exactly `size / grid` again. `fit: preserve` is no answer: it
// ignores the viewbox, so it only fits when size == grid.
